Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0000
Subject: script: don't crash without a console viewer

A display has no console viewer when text rendering is unavailable (no label plugin) or
plymouth.prefer-fbcon is set, but the sprite library's first full redraw called
ply_console_viewer_show/hide on it regardless: the daemon died with SIGSEGV as the script theme
started. The two-step plugin already checks for NULL here.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/plugins/splash/script/script-lib-sprite.c b/src/plugins/splash/script/script-lib-sprite.c
--- a/src/plugins/splash/script/script-lib-sprite.c
+++ b/src/plugins/splash/script/script-lib-sprite.c
@@ -905,6 +905,8 @@
                      node;
                      node = ply_list_get_next_node (data->displays, node)) {
                         script_lib_display_t *display = ply_list_node_get_data (node);
+                        if (display->console_viewer == NULL)
+                                continue;
                         if (data->should_show_console_messages == true) {
                                 ply_console_viewer_show (display->console_viewer, display->pixel_display);
                         } else {
